> **SELF-EXCLUSION.** As of 2026-11-14, GPT-6.2 Sol is a **canary (灰度) model** that is being quietly routed to some Codex/ChatGPT users but has **no launch post, model card, API docs page, official price or benchmark suite** from OpenAI (verified against OpenAI's news feed and developer docs the same day). With zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact ID, no 1–100 scores are filed; the notes below record what is verified and what is leak/review-grade.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** GPT-6.2 Sol (canary identifier; not an official product name yet)
- **Short description:** OpenAI's expected next-generation mid-tier model (the GPT-6.2 family companion to the 6.2 Astra flagship), reported from ~2026-11-09 to be silently canary-launched ("悄悄灰度上线") — some users found themselves routed to it inside Codex/ChatGPT. Community canary reviews describe it as a large leap over GPT-6.1 Sol, unusually quota-efficient, and — per reviewers — competitive with or ahead of the GPT-6 Astra flagship on front-end/creative tasks. Official launch was still pending as of 2026-11-14 (a widely-circulated rumor pointed at a Thursday release).
- **Provider / access:** none official. Canary routing in Codex/ChatGPT; identifiers surfaced briefly in Google Cloud Console quota configurations alongside `gpt-6.2-astra` on 2026-11-04 (retracted within hours); no public API listing as of 2026-11-14.
- **Release / knowledge:** unreleased as of 2026-11-14 (OpenAI news RSS last checked 2026-11-14 shows no GPT-6.2 announcement; no `developers.openai.com` model page for the ID — both verified).
- **IDs:** `gpt-6.2-sol` (canary/telemetry identifier; absent from public API docs).
- **Context window:** not published (GPT-6.1 Sol: 1,050,000 — do not assume for 6.2).
- **Modalities:** not published (expect text/image like the Sol line; unverified).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** not announced. Community canary reports note heavy quota efficiency (one reviewer: ~10 runs consumed under 10% of a $200 Pro plan's quota window); GPT-6.1 Sol's official price is $2/$10 per 1M.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed; press summaries say Sol was trained in the same RL-heavy pipeline as the 6.2 flagship (not a distilled lightweight) — unverified.

